\pard\sa240 September 11, 2026\par
\pard\sa200 Dear IOActive Hiring Team,\par
\pard\sa200 I am applying for the Associate Security Consultant role. I am a career-changer moving deliberately into offensive security, and rather than ask you to take that on faith, I have made my work public: sudoanthony.github.io documents a full application penetration testing methodology, finding by finding, the way a client report reads. IOActive's research-fueled, attacker's-perspective approach - and your mobile and hardware focus in particular - is exactly the environment I have been teaching myself toward.\par
\pard\sa200 The centerpiece of my portfolio is an end-to-end methodology across all ten OWASP Mobile Top 10 (2024) risks, tested against the intentionally vulnerable apps AllSafe, InsecureBankv2, and AndroGoat and mapped to the OWASP MASVS/MASTG. I worked it the way this role describes: static analysis in jadx and apktool, dynamic instrumentation with Frida and objection, traffic interception with certificate-pinning bypass in Burp Suite, and native-library reversing in Ghidra to recover a hardcoded password. Every issue - exported components and deep links, SQL injection in content providers, insecure storage and broken cryptography, a client-side biometric bypass, and root-detection defeat - is written up as a finding with a CVSS v3.1 vector, a CWE, business impact, and remediation. That last part matters to me as much as the exploit: a finding a client can actually act on is the deliverable.\par
\pard\sa200 I will not overstate my experience - I am early in this field, and this is a role I would grow into working alongside your consultants. What I bring next to the technical work is seven years as a U.S. Navy Hospital Corpsman, where precision, discipline around sensitive information, and clear communication under pressure were the job, plus 300+ hours teaching complex material to hundreds of people. In a recent software QA role I found, reproduced, and documented defects every day - the same reflexes this position asks for. I am bilingual in English and Japanese, remote-ready, and I move quickly when I am learning something I care about; the portfolio is the evidence of that.\par
\pard\sa240 I would welcome the chance to talk about how I can contribute to your engagements while I keep building, including pursuing the OSCP as I go. Thank you for considering me, and for the work IOActive does - I would be glad to be one of "the good guys" on your team.\par
\pard\sa0 Sincerely,\par
\pard Anthony Sciuto\par
